# Valid Parentheses

LeetCode Problem: Valid Parentheses
Difficulty: Easy

## Approach

Used a Stack (Deque) to keep track of opening brackets.

- If the character is an opening bracket, push it into the stack.
- If the character is a closing bracket:
  - If the stack is empty, the parentheses are invalid.
  - Otherwise, check whether the top opening bracket matches the closing bracket.
  - If it matches, pop the opening bracket.
  - If it doesn't match, return false.
- At the end, the stack must be empty for the parentheses to be valid.

## Complexity

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n)

SOLUTION :
import java.util.ArrayDeque;
import java.util.Deque;

class Solution {
    public boolean isValid(String s) {
        Deque<Character> dq = new ArrayDeque<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

            if (s.charAt(i) == '[' || s.charAt(i) == '{' || s.charAt(i) == '(') {
                dq.push(s.charAt(i));
            } else {
                if (dq.isEmpty()) {
                    return false;
                }

                if ((dq.peek() == '(' && s.charAt(i) == ')') ||
                    (dq.peek() == '[' && s.charAt(i) == ']') ||
                    (dq.peek() == '{' && s.charAt(i) == '}')) {

                    dq.pop();
                } else {
                    return false;
                }
            }
        }

        return dq.isEmpty();
    }
}
